CLICKDEAD-xhci — the fourth pointer counter: the dup-Success guard's SILENT exit.
=================================================================================

LANE. `unaos/crates/kernel/src/drivers/xhci/mod.rs` is rmbp's lane (CLAUDE.md §Worktrees).
This hunk is therefore delivered as a patch and is NOT committed to that file; the orin
branch `exec-orin15-clickdead2` carries `drivers/xhci/mod.rs` byte-identical to trunk
(`git diff f49ea1e7 -- unaos/crates/kernel/src/drivers/xhci/mod.rs` -> 0 lines). Asked of
rmbp as `GRANT xhci/mod.rs`, the way A17 asked for `prtscr.rs`.

APPLY.  git apply docs/dev/evidence/orin15/CLICKDEAD-xhci.patch
Base: 2de4a58b (`aarch64/tegra: CLICKDEAD — …`), whose `drivers/xhci/mod.rs` == trunk
f49ea1e7's. The second file, `arch/aarch64/display_tegra.rs`, IS orin's lane, but its `dup`
hunks ride HERE and not in the commit for one reason: they name `MOUSE_DUP_DROP_COUNT`,
which does not exist until the first file's hunk lands. Splitting them would leave the
branch unbuildable. Apply both or neither.

THE MECHANISM, NAMED. Not "a TRB is not re-queued" — a COMPLETION IS CONSUMED AND THE READ
IS NEVER RE-ARMED, and the discard is silent. At `2de4a58b:XhciController::poll_events`,
in the pointer arm guarded by `mouse_dci == Some(endpoint_id)` (mod.rs:4560), the
dup-Success guard fires when `slot.mouse_expect_phys != 0 && param != slot.mouse_expect_phys`
(mod.rs:4587). Inside it, `2de4a58b:XhciController::queue_mouse_read` (mod.rs:14846) is called
ONLY under `param != prev && have_buf` (mod.rs:4594). The complement —
`param == slot.mouse_prev_phys` (the known Panther-Point duplicate Success for the TD already
consumed, XHCI_SPURIOUS_SUCCESS / device 0x1e31), OR `slot.mouse_data_buffer` /
`slot.mouse_ring` gone — falls through to the bare `return;` at mod.rs:4599. That branch:

  * consumes the transfer event (the ring dequeue pointer has already advanced),
  * does NOT call `queue_mouse_read`, so no new interrupt-IN TD is enqueued on the pointer
    DCI and no doorbell rings — the endpoint is left with nothing armed,
  * and prints NOTHING on the flight build, because its only witness,
    `2de4a58b:XhciController::piusb39_witness` (mod.rs:14730-14731), is
    `#[cfg(feature = "usbdebug")]` and `usbdebug` is absent from the Orin flight recipe
    (witness,ehcihid,holocron,tegra,orinclick,tegra_el0,tegrasmp,orinrender,
    desktop_firmware,orinrx,tcuprobe,deskcascade).

Every OTHER exit accounts for itself: `2de4a58b:MOUSE_REARM_COUNT` (mod.rs:2373) on every
`queue_mouse_read`, `2de4a58b:MOUSE_DISCARD_REARM_COUNT` (mod.rs:2378) on the guard's
re-arming exit, `2de4a58b:MOUSE_ERROR_REARM_COUNT` (mod.rs:2385) on the non-halting error
re-arm, and halting completions go to `2de4a58b:XhciController::hid_error_witness`
(mod.rs:14748), which is UNGATED. So this one branch is the whole blind spot, and on the
wire it is INDISTINGUISHABLE from "the controller posted no transfer event at all" — which
is exactly the ambiguity render6 died in (`docs/dev/evidence/orin15/render6-boot1.log`:
`:: MOUSE-1: 1 reports ::` once at line 286 and never again, zero `hid_error_witness` lines,
zero `JD20 — pointer BUTTON`).

WHAT THE PATCH ADDS. `MOUSE_DUP_DROP_COUNT`, a fourth ungated `pub AtomicU64` bumped on
exactly that branch, and the `dup=` field + `DUP-DROP` verdict that
`2de4a58b:ptrpoll_witness` (display_tegra.rs:5111) prints from it. It also folds `dup` into
the witness's movement test — without that, a pipeline being EATEN (rearm flat, dup climbing)
would be silently mistaken for one that is STARVED and print one line for the whole boot.
After this patch the two live sub-mechanisms are separated on a single line:

  `-> DUP-DROP`            = (a1) completions arrive; the guard eats them without re-arming.
  `-> ARMED-NO-COMPLETION` = (a2) dup=0; the endpoint posted nothing. Look at EP state, the
                             doorbell and periodic bandwidth, not at the guard.

The patch is DIAGNOSTIC ONLY. It does not change the guard's control flow — the dup hazard
is real (re-arming on a genuine duplicate over-arms the interrupt-IN ring, the UI1-MOUSE M2
hazard) and PIUSB-39's discrimination stays exactly as it is. It adds one relaxed
`fetch_add` and one relaxed load. No lock, no MMIO.

LINE-NEUTRAL — YES. BYTE-NEUTRAL ON THE PI IMAGE — NO, AND THAT IS THE COST OF THE GRANT.
Two separate claims, both measured, and an earlier draft of this header conflated them.

  * LINE-neutral, verified. `drivers/xhci/mod.rs` is compiled into the Pi's `kernel8.img`,
    and a line added anywhere in it moves every `panic::Location` below (MEMORY: "cfg does
    not protect byte identity"). Both of its hunks are therefore FOLDED ONTO EXISTING LINES:
    `wc -l` reads **14917 patched == 14917 unpatched**. Nothing moves. `display_tegra.rs`
    gains 2 lines, but both are past its old tail (5032), so nothing pre-existing moves
    there either.
  * BYTE-neutral on `kernel8.img` — it is NOT, and the patch must not pretend otherwise:
        knob-off `./arroyo kernel8` unpatched -> d73a8981d65bd24e254567934f0f2d21b3307b4a761408618d576623e2669fb0
        knob-off `./arroyo kernel8` patched   -> 41eda903e85796d3564fded936613a8616780d81e9d9c0d5dc7110bb3d247198
        both 1254984 bytes — same SIZE, different CONTENT.
    The reason is deliberate, not accidental: `MOUSE_DUP_DROP_COUNT` and its `fetch_add` are
    UNGATED, exactly like the three siblings they join (`MOUSE_REARM_COUNT`,
    `MOUSE_DISCARD_REARM_COUNT`, `MOUSE_ERROR_REARM_COUNT`, mod.rs:2373-2385). Gating them
    on `orinclick` would put an orin-named knob in a shared driver, which
    MEMORY:"name by subsystem, not board" forbids; gating them on `usbdebug` would rebuild
    the very blind spot this patch exists to close. So the patch costs every aarch64 image
    one 8-byte BSS atomic and one relaxed increment on the pointer-completion path — no new
    file bytes (the size is unchanged), no lock, no MMIO, no control-flow change.

    **This is the whole substance of what rmbp is being asked to grant, and it is why the
    hunk is a patch and not a commit.** A reviewer who wants the accounting without touching
    the Pi's image should say so; the alternative is a `usbdebug`-gated counter that cannot
    answer render7's question on the flight recipe.

The knob-off `kernel8.img` sha for the COMMITTED work (this patch NOT applied) is unchanged
by CLICKDEAD: d73a8981…9fb0 before and after `2de4a58b`. See CLICKDEAD.md §6.

